package CanvasNet {
    part def ThemeResolver {
        doc /* The internal static ThemeResolver (partial class in ThemeResolver.cs and one file per theme) with the JavaScript object model ThemeObject and Js, the flowchart style sheet FlowchartStyles with ShapePaint and TextPaint over the UnifiedStyles base of the diagrams drawn by the unified renderer (the selectors the Rendering units read) and the DiagramStyles base that holds the global rules shared by every style sheet (ThemeResolver.Styles.cs), the class style sheet ClassStyles (ThemeResolver.DiagramStyles.cs), and the sequence style sheet SequenceStyles with ShadowPaint (ThemeResolver.SequenceStyles.cs). GetThemeVariables ports Mermaid's getThemeVariables for the five built-in themes default, base, dark, forest, and neutral: the constructor's base values, calculate (the default theme first resets every calculated placeholder), the overrides copied in, every color derived in updateColors in the class's own order with the khroma port ColorMath, and the overrides copied in again so that an overridden derived variable wins; overrides that are not an object are ignored. Every variable of every diagram type is computed, so the result equals Mermaid's object variable for variable. ThemeObject behaves as the JavaScript this of a theme class (undefined, the || and ?? fallbacks, member access, insertion order, and the JSON.stringify form). The color-scale loops that THEME_COLOR_LIMIT controls are capped at 64 iterations; a value that is not a color fails with a ColorFormatException that carries it, and an unsupported theme throws ArgumentException. The neo and redux themes of the pinned Mermaid are not ported. FlowchartStyles.Create builds the global rules of Mermaid's getStyles and the flowchart's styles.ts from the theme variables of a MermaidConfig as selector-keyed rules (only the declarations that change pixels, a declaration with an invalid value dropped as a browser drops it), appends the themeCSS rules of the flowchart's own selectors (an important theme declaration staying in effect) and reports every other themeCSS rule as mermaid-theme-css-unsupported, and resolves the paints of nodes, subgraphs, edges, markers, labels, the title, and the edge label background. SequenceStyles.Create builds the same global rules and the sequence rules of Mermaid's styles.js, appends the themeCSS rules of the sequence diagram's own selectors (reporting the others in the same way), and resolves the cascade over the attributes Mermaid gives each element, from least to most specific: shapes, lines (the line rule's 2 pixels, beaten by the message rules), text colors, shadows, boxes, and message lines, with typed paints for lifelines, frame lines, label boxes, markers, sequence numbers, and the drop shadows of boxes and menu panels (a CSS filter of none or one drop-shadow()). ClassStyles.Create builds the same global rules and the class rules of Mermaid's class styles.js, appends the themeCSS rules of the class diagram's own selectors (reporting the others), and resolves the paints of class boxes and dividers, namespaces, node, note, edge, and terminal labels, the edge label backgrounds, the relation markers, and the title in the root font. The types are stateless or immutable. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.Default.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.Base.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.Dark.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.Forest.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.Neutral.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.Styles.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.SequenceStyles.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Configuration/ThemeResolver.DiagramStyles.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid.Tests/Configuration/ThemeResolverTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid.Tests/Fixtures/upstream-vectors/themes.json */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-mermaid/configuration/theme-resolver.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-mermaid/configuration/theme-resolver.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-mermaid/configuration/theme-resolver.yaml */
    }
}
